WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.301 --> 00:00:03.936
-The president is ratcheting up
his trade war with China

00:00:03.936 --> 00:00:05.405
and lying about what it means

00:00:05.405 --> 00:00:07.206
for American companies
and consumers.

00:00:07.206 --> 00:00:09.142
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:09.142 --> 00:00:10.743
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:10.743 --> 00:00:13.513 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:13.513 --> 00:00:14.881
When it comes to foreign policy,

00:00:14.881 --> 00:00:16.583
there are two things we know
about Donald Trump.

00:00:16.583 --> 00:00:18.351
He wants to be liked by everyone

00:00:18.351 --> 00:00:20.653
and he has no idea what he's
talking about.

00:00:20.653 --> 00:00:23.422
That's why his description
of how he would conduct himself

00:00:23.422 --> 00:00:25.291
in office was always
so incoherent.

00:00:25.291 --> 00:00:26.692
During the campaign,
for example,

00:00:26.692 --> 00:00:29.062
Trump insisted both that
as a businessman,

00:00:29.062 --> 00:00:30.930
he could have good relationships
with everybody

00:00:30.930 --> 00:00:34.500
and also that, as a nation,
we should be unpredictable.

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:37.003
-As a businessman, I get along
with everybody.

00:00:37.003 --> 00:00:38.437
I have business
all over the world.

00:00:38.437 --> 00:00:42.976
We must, as a nation, be more
unpredictable.

00:00:42.976 --> 00:00:44.511
We are totally predictable.

00:00:44.511 --> 00:00:47.246
We have to be unpredictable.

00:00:47.246 --> 00:00:49.582
-No. You can't get along
with everybody

00:00:49.582 --> 00:00:51.217
and also be unpredictable.

00:00:51.217 --> 00:00:54.787
Nobody likes
their unpredictable friend.

00:00:54.787 --> 00:00:56.722
Trump's like guy
who won't respond to texts

00:00:56.722 --> 00:00:58.324
when you ask him for a ride
to the airport,

00:00:58.324 --> 00:01:00.393
but then he shows up at your
door at 3:00 a.m.

00:01:00.393 --> 00:01:02.295
with a handle of vodka
and a duffel bag.

00:01:02.295 --> 00:01:03.830
And when you say, "Go home,"
he's like,

00:01:03.830 --> 00:01:06.199
[ As Trump ] "I can't. I got
stoned and sold my apartment."

00:01:06.199 --> 00:01:07.366
[ Laughter ]

00:01:07.366 --> 00:01:08.500
[ Normal voice ]
Now we're seeing what

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:10.136
Trump's unpredictability
looks like

00:01:10.136 --> 00:01:12.138
when it comes to imposing
tariffs on China.

00:01:12.138 --> 00:01:14.407
China retaliated this week
with tariffs

00:01:14.407 --> 00:01:16.409
and the escalating trade wars
hurt farmers

00:01:16.409 --> 00:01:17.911
and sent the stock market
plummeting.

00:01:17.911 --> 00:01:20.046
And yet, Trump has repeatedly
shrugged it off,

00:01:20.046 --> 00:01:22.815
claiming our economy is strong
enough to handle a trade war

00:01:22.815 --> 00:01:25.151
and insisting it's not
that big of a deal.

00:01:25.151 --> 00:01:29.255
-So the economy is doing
very well by every measure.

00:01:29.255 --> 00:01:31.624
We are having probably
the greatest economy

00:01:31.624 --> 00:01:32.959
that we have had anywhere,

00:01:32.959 --> 00:01:36.563
anytime in the history
of our country.

00:01:36.563 --> 00:01:39.832
We are having a little squabble
with China

00:01:39.832 --> 00:01:42.168
because we have been treated
very unfairly

00:01:42.168 --> 00:01:43.703
for many, many decades.

00:01:43.703 --> 00:01:45.938
-A little squabble
is not how you describe

00:01:45.938 --> 00:01:48.041
a trade war with the world's
second largest economy.

00:01:48.041 --> 00:01:50.877
That's language your dad uses
when he explains

00:01:50.877 --> 00:01:54.480
why he's been sleeping in
a motel for the past few weeks.

00:01:54.480 --> 00:01:56.716
"Your mom and I are having
a little squabble

00:01:56.716 --> 00:01:59.251
over a photo of daddy
at a big boys' party

00:01:59.251 --> 00:02:01.220
with a lady
who popped out of a cake.

00:02:01.220 --> 00:02:02.221
[ Laughter ]

00:02:02.221 --> 00:02:04.690
It's a squabble.
It'll be over soon."

00:02:04.690 --> 00:02:07.026
Even some Democrats have been
in favor of using tariffs

00:02:07.026 --> 00:02:09.395
as a temporary tool to get a
long-term deal with China

00:02:09.395 --> 00:02:10.796
that helps American workers.

00:02:10.796 --> 00:02:13.632
But one of those Democrats,
Ohio Senator Sherrod Brown,

00:02:13.632 --> 00:02:15.901
expressed concern that Trump
was using the tariffs

00:02:15.901 --> 00:02:17.303
as a permanent solution.

00:02:17.303 --> 00:02:19.271
-I am very concerned
that the president

00:02:19.271 --> 00:02:22.242
has not understood that tariffs

00:02:22.242 --> 00:02:26.312
need to be a short-term tool
to get to a long-term policy.

00:02:26.312 --> 00:02:29.115
He seems to think the tariffs
are the policy.

00:02:29.115 --> 00:02:32.351
-Yeah. Tariffs are supposed
to be a temporary punishment,

00:02:32.351 --> 00:02:33.720
not a permanent solution.

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:35.921
It's like if your kid
doesn't do their chores,

00:02:35.921 --> 00:02:37.556
you send them to their room
for an hour.

00:02:37.556 --> 00:02:40.593
You don't make them live there
for 30 years.

00:02:40.593 --> 00:02:41.994
That's probably why these two

00:02:41.994 --> 00:02:43.529
looks like they have
never seen the daylight.

00:02:43.529 --> 00:02:44.597
[ Laughter ]

00:02:44.597 --> 00:02:49.568
And then...
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:49.568 --> 00:02:51.237
-...there are the Republicans

00:02:51.237 --> 00:02:52.871
who have traditionally
opposed tariffs

00:02:52.871 --> 00:02:54.140
and supported free trade.

00:02:54.140 --> 00:02:56.409
Suddenly those Republicans
have gone very quiet.

00:02:56.409 --> 00:02:58.878
And even when they express
mild concern to Trump,

00:02:58.878 --> 00:03:00.446
their message
doesn't seem to get through,

00:03:00.446 --> 00:03:02.314
like Iowa Senator Chuck Grassley

00:03:02.314 --> 00:03:04.917
who represents a lot of farmers
hurt by Trump's tariffs.

00:03:04.917 --> 00:03:06.919
Grassley told
"The Washington Post" yesterday

00:03:06.919 --> 00:03:08.654
that he planned to write
a letter to Trump

00:03:08.654 --> 00:03:10.322
to explain the concerns
of farmers

00:03:10.322 --> 00:03:12.891
because he felt the argument
he had repeatedly made

00:03:12.891 --> 00:03:14.927
to the president in person
was not registering.

00:03:14.927 --> 00:03:16.996
I'm not sure if you
talk to him face to face

00:03:16.996 --> 00:03:18.931
he hears everything you say.

00:03:18.931 --> 00:03:22.535
And I do believe he doesn't hear
everything face to face.

00:03:22.535 --> 00:03:25.004
I mean, have you ever seen
the way he looks in a meeting

00:03:25.004 --> 00:03:26.606
when someone else is talking?

00:03:26.606 --> 00:03:29.308
He hates it so much,
he literally hugs himself

00:03:29.308 --> 00:03:31.711
as a calming mechanism.

00:03:31.711 --> 00:03:32.979
[ As Trump ]
Don't worry, Donald.

00:03:32.979 --> 00:03:34.580
The bad man will be done soon,

00:03:34.580 --> 00:03:37.984
and then it will be your turn
to make noise with your mouth.

00:03:37.984 --> 00:03:40.620
[ Laughter ]

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:42.922
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:42.922 --> 00:03:45.625
[ Normal voice ]
So now Trump has us mired

00:03:45.625 --> 00:03:46.892
in a damaging trade war

00:03:46.892 --> 00:03:48.460
with the world's
second largest economy

00:03:48.460 --> 00:03:50.863
that's pissing off both parties
and has no end in sight.

00:03:50.863 --> 00:03:52.798
But as usual, he keeps insisting

00:03:52.798 --> 00:03:54.667
that even though he
and the president of China

00:03:54.667 --> 00:03:57.136
are fighting,
they still get along great.

00:03:57.136 --> 00:04:00.672
-The relationship I have with
President Xi is extraordinary.

00:04:00.672 --> 00:04:02.007
It's really very good,

00:04:02.007 --> 00:04:05.311
but he's for China,
and I'm for the USA.

00:04:05.311 --> 00:04:08.447
-And honestly, I'm just relieved
he knows what side he's on.

00:04:08.447 --> 00:04:11.017
Trump's like a kid
in a youth soccer game

00:04:11.017 --> 00:04:13.186
who gets confused about
what team he's on

00:04:13.186 --> 00:04:14.654
and kicks it into the wrong goal

00:04:14.654 --> 00:04:17.089
and Republicans are like
the helicopter parents

00:04:17.089 --> 00:04:18.824
on the sideline
who cheer for him anyway.

00:04:18.824 --> 00:04:21.060
"Yes, Bradley,
you choose whatever goal

00:04:21.060 --> 00:04:23.295
you feel comfortable with!"

00:04:23.295 --> 00:04:24.329
But you've got to give it
to Trump.

00:04:24.329 --> 00:04:25.464
You've got to give it to Trump.

00:04:25.464 --> 00:04:27.132
He might not know
how tariffs work,

00:04:27.132 --> 00:04:30.403
but he definitely knows which
country he is the president of.

00:04:30.403 --> 00:04:33.639
-President Xi,
he's a friend of mine.

00:04:33.639 --> 00:04:35.475
And I'm a friend of his
and I like him a lot,

00:04:35.475 --> 00:04:37.109
but he's representing China,

00:04:37.109 --> 00:04:39.912
and I'm representing
the United States of America.

00:04:39.912 --> 00:04:43.749
President Xi is for China.
And I'm for the United States.

00:04:43.749 --> 00:04:46.952
He's representing China, and I'm
representing the United States.

00:04:46.952 --> 00:04:50.589
He represents China.
I represent the USA.

00:04:50.589 --> 00:04:52.992
He likes China,
and I like the United States.

00:04:52.992 --> 00:04:54.694
He's for China. I'm for us.

00:04:54.694 --> 00:04:57.429
President Xi,
he's a friend of mine,

00:04:57.429 --> 00:04:58.764
but he likes China.

00:04:58.764 --> 00:05:00.166
I like the USA.

00:05:00.166 --> 00:05:02.968
-We all know that!

00:05:02.968 --> 00:05:06.539
This is like if Steph Curry held
a post-game press conference

00:05:06.539 --> 00:05:08.374
and just went,
"I play for the Warriors.

00:05:08.374 --> 00:05:10.409
James Harden plays
for the Rockets. Goodbye."

00:05:10.409 --> 00:05:12.578
[ Laughter ]

00:05:12.578 --> 00:05:15.348
Now tariffs are basically --

00:05:15.348 --> 00:05:19.185
basically tariffs are a tax
on imports from that country.

00:05:19.185 --> 00:05:22.187
So the American companies
importing those goods

00:05:22.187 --> 00:05:24.790
pay the tax, and they often
end up passing that tax

00:05:24.790 --> 00:05:27.159
on to consumers, and yet Trump
keeps repeating the lie

00:05:27.159 --> 00:05:29.061
that China will pay the tariffs

00:05:29.061 --> 00:05:31.263
rather than American companies
and consumers.

00:05:31.263 --> 00:05:34.167
He did it again last week
while simultaneously claiming

00:05:34.167 --> 00:05:36.469
once again that he has
a great relationship

00:05:36.469 --> 00:05:37.703
with the president of China.

00:05:37.703 --> 00:05:39.338
-We were getting very close
to a deal.

00:05:39.338 --> 00:05:41.173
Then they started
to renegotiate the deal.

00:05:41.173 --> 00:05:43.375
We can't have that.
We can't have that.

00:05:43.375 --> 00:05:47.179
So our country can take in
$120 billion a year in tariffs

00:05:47.179 --> 00:05:50.015
paid for mostly by China,
by the way, not by us.

00:05:50.015 --> 00:05:52.618
A lot of people try and steer it
in a different direction.

00:05:52.618 --> 00:05:56.021
Ultimately, it's paid for
largely by China.

00:05:56.021 --> 00:05:58.924
-Do you have plans to talk to
President Xi, or no, not yet?

00:05:58.924 --> 00:06:00.659
-Well, he just wrote me
a beautiful letter.

00:06:00.659 --> 00:06:04.663
I just received it, and I'll
probably speak to him by phone.

00:06:04.663 --> 00:06:08.167
-Okay. First of all, you'll
probably speak to him by phone?

00:06:08.167 --> 00:06:10.502
If someone sends you
a beautiful letter,

00:06:10.502 --> 00:06:12.037
you call them.

00:06:12.037 --> 00:06:13.505
That is just basic etiquette.

00:06:13.505 --> 00:06:15.441
One time, my grandma sent me
a birthday card.

00:06:15.441 --> 00:06:17.442
I didn't call her right away,
and later that day,

00:06:17.442 --> 00:06:19.679
I got another card slipped under
my door that said,

00:06:19.679 --> 00:06:21.714
"No phone call?"

00:06:21.714 --> 00:06:25.751
And she included a bill
for the $5.

00:06:25.751 --> 00:06:27.220
Second,
Trump has the weird thing

00:06:27.220 --> 00:06:30.423
where he's obsessed with getting
beautiful letters from people.

00:06:30.423 --> 00:06:32.091
He said it multiple times
about everyone

00:06:32.091 --> 00:06:33.959
from Kim Jong-un
to Vladimir Putin

00:06:33.959 --> 00:06:35.761
to the former Director
of National Intelligence,

00:06:35.761 --> 00:06:37.530
James Clapper,
and even President Obama

00:06:37.530 --> 00:06:38.998
shortly after he took office.

00:06:38.998 --> 00:06:41.834
-"James Clapper, who famously
got caught lying to Congress,

00:06:41.834 --> 00:06:44.036
is now an authority
on Donald Trump.

00:06:44.036 --> 00:06:46.238
Will he show you his beautiful
letter to me?"

00:06:46.238 --> 00:06:47.874
-Putin even sent me a present,

00:06:47.874 --> 00:06:50.309
a beautiful present
with a beautiful note.

00:06:50.309 --> 00:06:54.346
-A letter was given to me
by Kim Jong-un,

00:06:54.346 --> 00:06:57.116
and that letter
was a very nice letter.

00:06:57.116 --> 00:06:59.218
Oh, would you like to see
what was in that letter.

00:06:59.218 --> 00:07:04.556
-I just showed a letter
that I received just yesterday

00:07:04.556 --> 00:07:07.693
from Chairman Kim which
is an extraordinary letter.

00:07:07.693 --> 00:07:10.896
-I just went to the oval office

00:07:10.896 --> 00:07:15.768
and found this beautiful letter
from President Obama.

00:07:15.768 --> 00:07:18.036
-This was the letter

00:07:18.036 --> 00:07:20.473
given to me by President Obama.

00:07:20.473 --> 00:07:24.176
It was long. It was complex.

00:07:24.176 --> 00:07:25.711
It was thoughtful.

00:07:25.711 --> 00:07:27.613
-[ As Trump ] And I didn't
understand a word of it.

00:07:27.613 --> 00:07:29.114
[ Laughter ]

00:07:29.114 --> 00:07:30.449
I just know...

00:07:30.449 --> 00:07:35.220
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:35.220 --> 00:07:36.989
I just know it was...

00:07:36.989 --> 00:07:40.092
It was shaped like this.

00:07:40.092 --> 00:07:41.593
[ Normal voice ]
His obsession with letters

00:07:41.593 --> 00:07:43.963
makes him sound like
a Civil War wife.

00:07:43.963 --> 00:07:45.831
[ Older Southern accent ] I just
got the most beautiful letter

00:07:45.831 --> 00:07:47.867
from Beauregard.

00:07:47.867 --> 00:07:49.801
[ Laughter ]

00:07:49.801 --> 00:07:51.604
[ Normal voice ]
Also, why is Trump

00:07:51.604 --> 00:07:55.107
always carrying
these letters around?

00:07:55.107 --> 00:07:57.342
Is that why his coat's
always so bulky?

00:07:57.342 --> 00:08:01.747
He's just packed full of mail
everywhere he goes?

00:08:01.747 --> 00:08:04.149
Terrible president, but he'd
make a great mailman.

00:08:04.149 --> 00:08:06.319
I can totally see him --
shorts, high socks,

00:08:06.319 --> 00:08:08.020
tugging around a mail sack.

00:08:08.020 --> 00:08:13.425
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:13.425 --> 00:08:15.027
But the important part
of that clip

00:08:15.027 --> 00:08:16.962
is the part where Trump claimed
that China

00:08:16.962 --> 00:08:18.530
and not the U.S. companies
would pay the tariff.

00:08:18.530 --> 00:08:20.132
It's a lie he's been repeating
for years.

00:08:20.132 --> 00:08:22.301
And on Sunday,
Fox host Chris Wallace

00:08:22.301 --> 00:08:24.971
got Trump's chief economic
advisor, Larry Kudlow,

00:08:24.971 --> 00:08:26.639
to admit that it was a lie.

00:08:26.639 --> 00:08:29.942
-It's not China that pays
tariffs.

00:08:29.942 --> 00:08:32.177
It's the American importers,

00:08:32.177 --> 00:08:34.947
the American companies
that pay what, in effect,

00:08:34.947 --> 00:08:36.314
is a tax increase,

00:08:36.314 --> 00:08:39.218
and oftentimes, passes it on
to U.S. consumers.

00:08:39.218 --> 00:08:42.287
-Fair enough. In fact,
both sides will pay.

00:08:42.287 --> 00:08:45.524
Both sides will pay in these
things, and, of course --

00:08:45.524 --> 00:08:48.360
-If it's a tariff on goods
coming into the country,

00:08:48.360 --> 00:08:49.996
the Chinese aren't paying.

00:08:49.996 --> 00:08:53.765
-No. But the Chinese
will suffer GDP losses

00:08:53.765 --> 00:08:57.302
and so forth with respect
to a diminishing export market

00:08:57.302 --> 00:08:59.672
and goods that they may need
for their own --

00:08:59.672 --> 00:09:02.074
-I understand that,
but the president says

00:09:02.074 --> 00:09:04.943
China pays for the tariffs.

00:09:04.943 --> 00:09:06.345
They may suffer consequences,

00:09:06.345 --> 00:09:08.447
but it's U.S. businesses

00:09:08.447 --> 00:09:10.582
and U.S. consumers who pay,
correct?

00:09:10.582 --> 00:09:13.552
-Yes, to some extent.
I don't disagree with that.

00:09:13.552 --> 00:09:15.421
-Oh, Larry, you just admitted

00:09:15.421 --> 00:09:17.856
that Trump is a liar
on Fox News.

00:09:17.856 --> 00:09:19.358
You're gonna have to
apologize to him,

00:09:19.358 --> 00:09:21.193
and I have a feeling I know
how you'll do it.

00:09:21.193 --> 00:09:23.628
[ As Trump ] I just got
the most beautiful letter.

00:09:23.628 --> 00:09:26.666
Larry Kudlow says
I'm not a liar.

00:09:26.666 --> 00:09:30.202
Let me just find it
here in my mail coat.

00:09:30.202 --> 00:09:32.637
This one's from Putin.

00:09:32.637 --> 00:09:34.339
Obama. Oh!

00:09:34.339 --> 00:09:35.741
Pottery Barn.

00:09:35.741 --> 00:09:37.209
[ Laughter ]

00:09:37.209 --> 00:09:38.644
[ Normal voice ]
So Trump's antagonizing China

00:09:38.644 --> 00:09:40.212
in a costly trade war
that no one wants,

00:09:40.212 --> 00:09:41.980
Democrats and Republicans
are both unhappy,

00:09:41.980 --> 00:09:43.382
and the stock market
is plummeting.

00:09:43.382 --> 00:09:44.684
And it really seems like Trump

00:09:44.684 --> 00:09:46.218
is feeling increasingly isolated

00:09:46.218 --> 00:09:48.854
because during a speech to
workers in Louisiana yesterday,

00:09:48.854 --> 00:09:50.522
he went out of his way to insist

00:09:50.522 --> 00:09:52.958
that the U.S. doesn't need
any help from other countries.

00:09:52.958 --> 00:09:56.362
-You are not only making
our nation wealthier,

00:09:56.362 --> 00:09:59.098
but you are making America safer

00:09:59.098 --> 00:10:02.535
by building a future
of American energy independence.

00:10:02.535 --> 00:10:06.137
We are independent.
We don't need anybody.

00:10:06.137 --> 00:10:08.006
We don't need anybody.

00:10:08.006 --> 00:10:11.911
-Oh, boy. Really feels like
he's projecting there.

00:10:11.911 --> 00:10:14.012
Should be eating out of a tub
of ice cream

00:10:14.012 --> 00:10:15.614
on his sofa talking to his cat.

00:10:15.614 --> 00:10:18.617
[ As Trump ]
We don't need anybody.

00:10:18.617 --> 00:10:21.387
Isn't that right, Mike Pence?

00:10:21.387 --> 00:10:23.522
[ Laughter ]

00:10:23.522 --> 00:10:24.256
[ Applause ]

00:10:24.256 --> 00:10:28.026
Oh.

00:10:28.026 --> 00:10:29.694
Oh, that's a good boy.

00:10:29.694 --> 00:10:31.330
Oh, you're a good boy.

00:10:31.330 --> 00:10:33.799
You're a good boy, Mike Pence.
Yes.

00:10:33.799 --> 00:10:35.901
People say you're a boring,
dead-eyed cat,

00:10:35.901 --> 00:10:37.436
but I love you, Mike Pence.

00:10:37.436 --> 00:10:38.671
[ Laughter ]

00:10:38.671 --> 00:10:40.272
[ Normal voice ]
Even on his core issue,

00:10:40.272 --> 00:10:41.907
the thing that he claimed
he'd be able to fix,

00:10:41.907 --> 00:10:44.209
Trump has no strategy
and no idea what he's doing.

00:10:44.209 --> 00:10:46.278
He spent two years
talking about trade with China,

00:10:46.278 --> 00:10:47.279
and he's gotten nowhere.

00:10:47.279 --> 00:10:48.747
All we have are costly tariffs

00:10:48.747 --> 00:10:50.383
and the only thing Trump
knows for sure is...

00:10:50.383 --> 00:10:52.951
-He likes China. I like the USA.

00:10:52.951 --> 00:10:54.620
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:10:54.620 --> 00:10:55.988
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:10:55.988 --> 00:10:58.124 line:0%
♪♪

